+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Help & support · Ad Accelerator</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="popup.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="help.css"></head><body><main><header><span class="brand"><img src="icons/logo.svg" width="32" height="32" alt="">Ad Accelerator</span><span class="version">0.11.3</span></header><nav><a href="help.html">Help</a> · <a href="privacy-policy.html">Privacy policy</a> · <a href="licenses.html">Credits</a></nav><h1>Help & support</h1><p>Ad Accelerator is a free Chrome extension by Divyansh Kumar. It blocks listed ad and tracker destinations, hides common ad boxes, and tries to shorten detected video ads.</p><aside>The Chrome Web Store release is being prepared. There is no public store installation link yet. This extension requires Chrome 145 or later.</aside>
 <h2>Your everyday controls</h2><ol><li>Open a website and select Ad Accelerator from Chrome’s extensions menu. Pin it for quicker access.</li><li>Use <strong>Protection for this site</strong> to keep protection on or off for the current hostname and its subdomains. The choice is remembered.</li><li>Use <strong>Pause here for 10 minutes</strong> for a temporary break. Previously enabled site protections return when the timer ends. Reload to retry requests that were already blocked.</li><li>Under <strong>Video ads</strong>, choose a speed and whether to try skipping first. Normal playback speed is restored when the detected ad ends. The 20× option is a request; Chrome generally caps playback at 16× and players may allow less.</li></ol>
 <h2>If a page stops working</h2><p>Pause protection for that site and reload. For a smaller change, choose <strong>Page not working?</strong> and pause just the affected feature. Undo manually hidden boxes under <strong>My hidden elements</strong>.</p><p><strong>Strict navigation</strong> is optional. It restricts external destinations on a chosen site and can interrupt sign-ins or embedded players. Allow the exact destination or turn strict mode off, then reload.</p>
 <h2>What pausing means</h2><p>A full site pause suspends network filtering, page hiding, video assistance, popup cleanup, adaptive protection, strict navigation, tracking-link cleanup, and our location restrictions for matching sites. Saved preferences stay in place.</p><p>If you enabled our third-party cookie control, any full site pause or lasting exception also suspends that override <strong>across Chrome</strong>. It returns only after all full site pauses and exceptions end, if still enabled. Chrome’s own restrictions continue to apply. Filter-list updates have their own setting; pausing a site does not delete data or reverse prior deletions.</p>
