+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Privacy policy · Ad Accelerator</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="popup.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="help.css"></head><body><main><header><span class="brand"><img src="icons/logo.svg" width="32" height="32" alt="">Ad Accelerator</span><span class="version">0.11.3</span></header><nav><a href="help.html">Help</a> · <a href="privacy-policy.html">Privacy policy</a> · <a href="licenses.html">Credits</a></nav><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p class="updated">Effective September 6, 2026 · Ad Accelerator 0.11.3<br/>Developer: Divyansh Kumar · <a href="mailto:divyansh1032@gmail.com">divyansh1032@gmail.com</a></p><p>Ad Accelerator processes information in your browser to reduce ads, tracking, and unwanted popup navigation. The extension has no account system, analytics service, advertising, or developer-operated data collection server. It does not sell your data.</p>
 <h2>Information used in your browser</h2><p>The extension inspects website addresses, navigation events, links, visible page elements, and video-player state to apply protection. It can change page presentation and detected ad playback. It does not read passwords, payment fields, cookie values, or location coordinates. It does not request Chrome’s browsing-history permission.</p><p>Local extension storage contains settings, site exceptions, temporary pause times, strict-mode destinations, optional location-blocked origins, custom CSS selectors for elements you choose to hide, filter lists, and filter-update status. These settings are not synchronized or sent to the developer.</p>
 <h2>Automatic learning and temporary activity</h2><p>Adaptive protection stores up to 100 candidate or active rules and up to 100 temporary allow pairs locally. A rule contains source, destination and evidence hostnames, counts, timestamps and expiry. It does not persist full browsing URLs, query strings or page text. Rules expire 24 hours after first evidence; allow pairs expire after 24 hours. Expired rules are not enforced and are pruned periodically.</p><p>Pending popup chains may contain a source URL and tab identifiers in bounded worker memory for up to 10 seconds. Short-lived popup activity and navigation attempts are kept in memory or session storage, not uploaded. Private windows are excluded from adaptive learning. While you use the element picker, a source URL and a tab identifier can remain in session storage for up to five minutes to validate your selection.</p>
 <h2>Network connections</h2><p>The extension downloads three domain lists from HaGeZi’s public GitHub repository when you update filters or when enabled daily updates run. Those requests contain no browsing history, learned rules, cookie values, or page contents. The list host receives ordinary connection metadata, including your IP address. Downloads omit credentials and referrers. EasyList cosmetic filters are bundled with the extension. Downloaded lists are data, not executable code.</p><p>The extension does not proxy your browsing, hide your IP address, or prevent every form of tracking. Websites and their providers still receive ordinary traffic that is not blocked.</p>
